  "scope": "Worst velocity samples from the full standard comparison, not a separate full-grid audit.",
  "notes": [
    "The engine includes light time, annual aberration and nutation; solar gravitational deflection is not implemented. Its rapidly varying derivative near conjunction can be large while its position contribution is only arcseconds.",
    "The true-node Hermite table approximates positions and derivatives smoothly. At the sampled Swiss worst case, minute-scale finite differences and the returned speed differ strongly from 0.01-0.1 day finite differences. The table does not reproduce such short numerical features exactly.",
    "Standard-comparison errors and sign/retrograde disagreement counts are retained in the main audit; no samples are excluded."
  ],
